{
  "dom_id": "step-q51076",
  "name": "Question 19",
  "problem": "The following table shows the rate $r(t),$ in centimeters per hour, at which rain is falling during a two-hour period of a certain day.\n\n| $t\\,\\text{(hours)}$ | $0$ | $0.5$ | $1$ | $1.5$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $r\\,\\text{(centimeters/hour)}$ | $3$ | $4$ | $3$ | $3$ | $1$ |\n\nApproximate the total amount of rainfall during this period using the trapezoidal rule with $4$ trapezoids of equal height.",
  "worked_solution": "In this context, the area $A$ under the curve $y=r(t)$ over the interval $[0,2]$ represents the total amount of rainfall during the two-hour period.\n\nThe general formula for the trapezoidal rule states that\n\n$$\nA\u2248\\frac{1}{2}[r(a)+2(r({t}_{1})+r({t}_{2})+\u22ef+r({t}_{n-1}))+r(b)]\u0394t,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of trapezoids and $\u0394t=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ is the step size.\n\nHere, we have the following values:\n\n- The number of trapezoids is $n=4.$\n\n- The corresponding interval is $[0,2],$ so we have $a=0$ and $b=2.$\n\n- The step size is given by\n\n$$\n\u0394t=\\frac{b-a}{n}=\\frac{2-0}{4}=0.5.\n$$\n\nUsing the above values, the general formula becomes\n\n$$\nA\u2248\\frac{1}{2}[r(0)+2(r(0.5)+r(1)+r(1.5))+r(2)]\\cdot 0.5.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the appropriate numbers from the given table in the above expression gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & \u2248\\frac{1}{2}[3+2(4+3+3)+1]\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.25(24) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, approximately $6\\,\\text{cm}$ of rain fell during the given two-hour period.",
